  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is clearly the dominant modality (image_only resnet50: 0.208 vs rna_only: 0.485-0.650). Within RNA, multiprofile+avgpool is the best profile/aggregation setting (pca: 0.591 vs singleprofile: 0.485; avgpool: 0.591 vs transformer: 0.519), and scvi_n200 substantially outperforms pca_n2000 under identical settings (0.650 vs 0.591). This establishes a clear encoder ranking: scvi_n200 > pca_n2000. Question: Does scgpt, the third available RNA encoder, further improve on scvi_n200, or has encoder quality plateaued? config_008 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) holds profile setting and aggregation at their known-best values, isolating the encoder effect. This is the best use of the next experiment because it directly extends the strongest evidence (encoder choice drives the largest observed gap), requires no new assumptions about aggregation or profile interactions, and will determine whether to invest remaining budget in encoder exploration or pivot toward testing image/multimodal contributions."
}

